IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Writ Petition (Civil) No. 1362 of 2012
CITATION: 2024 SCC OnLine SC 150
YEAR: 2024

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, Sanjiv Khanna, B.R. Gavai, J.B. Pardiwala, Manoj Misra

PARTIES:
ADR vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India, Representation of the People Act, 1951, Companies Act, 2013

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 19(1)(a), Section 29C RPA

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
electoral bonds unconstitutional, voter right to information, political funding transparency

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Constitution bench struck down the Electoral Bond Scheme as unconstitutional under Article 19(1)(a), holding that voters have a fundamental right to know political contributors.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 19(1)(a), Section 29C RPA.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

